      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "The Carbon Border Adjustment Mechanism (CBAM) aims to reduce carbon leakage by imposing a carbon price on imported goods. The pros of CBAM include promoting global efforts to reduce emissions, supporting the transition to a low-carbon economy, and potentially driving innovation in greener technologies as foreign producers adapt. However, cons consist of possible trade disputes with non-EU countries, the risk of driving up consumer prices, and complexities in accurately measuring and enforcing carbon costs. Additionally, it may disadvantage EU exporters facing higher carbon costs. Both supporters and critics acknowledge that the effectiveness of CBAM relies on comprehensive and fair implementation.",
